Z||000000||JohnF||10-24-2001||08:13 AM||||Cruise didn't work - multi-function lever switch broken off.  Replaced lever assembly; cruise worked great for about 10 times.  <P>Any way to verify newly replaced stalk switch didn't fail before tearing into cruise system?<P>I have Rodney's cruise install/troubleshooting sheets.||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-24-2001||01:04 PM||||Yeah, you can check the stalk switch functions.  Unplug its connector from the cruise control module, and check it with a VOM.  It's just a couple switches and a rheostat, if I remember.  The connector is a flat thing that looks kind of like a spade lug, but it has four contact areas on it (two on each of the flat sides) - and it has a little hole in one corner.<P>The 4 wires going to the connector are real small, and are contained in a black plastic sheath; sort of like an old telephone line in your house.  You'll find it.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||10-24-2001||03:35 PM||||If I hold SET switch in, and ON/OFF switch is ON, on what color wires should I be able to get contiuity.  That should tell me if those two switches are working.<P>Then I can go from there, I think.||||reg||5
